  reason: "WHY RUST RATHER THAN .dag: the substrate has no directory enumeration sufficient to BIND each sibling `.dag` as a typed RecurringFailureMode value. Membership discovery exists (`v2.std.decl_index` `data_decl_type_facts`); value binding does not. Until that grounding lands, a checkout with no committed roster has no module for the three importers (`gunbc.design_ledgers`, `gunbc.ledger_row_coherence`, `test.claim.generated_artifact_merge_driver_real_execution_witness`) and the required parse join reports RosterModuleAbsent on the intended steady state. The host fold lists sibling files, writes gitignored roster.dag atomically, and refuses a shortened list. That is a §7 seed realization of a missing capability, not a scaffold: dissolution is grounded in gunbc.guarantee_stall.roster_re_enumerates_its_own_rows_stall (declaration-value binding), not in a sentence in the Rust module.\n\nThe file-versus-roster join arms are the other half of the same host: a skip in the writer must still refuse. They execute inside run_rostered_row_join on the required parse path (witnesses lane). file_roster_join_tests are the off-path REDs for those arms; they are enumerated because test items are still hand Rust.\n\nWHY ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE: gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing admits by PURPOSE. Removing the silent-drop constructor from the failure-mode ledger is an instrument tax every self-host lane was paying (merge hotspot). No new language behavior, no escape hatch, no emitted public surface.\n\nRe-derive this list with tools.seed_growth_change_population rather than maintaining a count.",
